      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stanton_Heights",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before becoming a neighborhood, the area was a private country club golf course—the largest in Pittsburgh until the mid‑1950s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stanton_Heights",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Stanton Heights was officially designated a Pittsburgh neighborhood only a little over fifty years ago.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.pittsburghbeautiful.com/2016/12/16/pittsburgh-neighborhoods-stanton-heights/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Sunnyside School, the neighborhood’s public school, features a pony‑sized ball field and playground just behind its building.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
